, "Incumbent Glenn Grothman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Glenn Grothman, the Republican incumbent, is seeking another term in a Wisconsin district that leans Republican by about eight points. His Democratic challenger, Brad Smith, won his primary in August and has the state AFL-CIO endorsement, but enters the general election with modest resources. Grothman has raised more than $900,000 and holds a large cash advantage, and he has used his office for visible constituent work such as pushing a disaster declaration for the district.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the seat Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a 6% chance. The only available poll, from May and sponsored by a Democratic-leaning firm, showed Grothman up by 22 points. The evidence points to an easy Republican hold, with Smith needing an unexpected wave to make this competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -10.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0701, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0353, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0532, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0212, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0386, "margin": -12.0}]}